 "vocab_version": "v04",
 "batch": "v07",
 "text_source": "captions_plus_linked_text",
 "notes": "Packet F1 is the uncaptioned TOC graphic; packet F2-F5 are paper Figs 1-4 (ids follow image files). Spine: gap -> hot-electron hypothesis -> Au/Al2O3/p-Si junction + bar arrays + resonance sweep + divide-and-fit method -> deposition -> lithography -> isolated bars -> ~2 eV localized plasmon -> plasmon-decay heating (MEC) -> two-slope T_e -> ATLE -> conclusion; control branch 1.3 eV device -> lower T_e (contrasts). Te(V) extrapolated onset at V~Eg (n15) and rectification (n11) are side claims. Supporting Information (Ti-thickness series, other bar geometries, spot-current linearity) is not in the packet. Consistency found: epsilon - V + phi_s = 0.26 eV at all four fitted voltages (F4 vs F5a), matching the 0.25 eV Delta line.",
